Add supervised and on-demand pod connections

Recover dead git tunnels as daemon-owned pod resources after transport
outages, tunnel process failures, and daemon restarts. Serialize
foreground and background setup so recovery cannot race a concurrent
enter.

Back off pod repair attempts and pause them after repeated failures
while the host remains reachable. A re-established shared host
connection immediately resumes every non-stopped pod on that host.
Back off unavailable host probes with jitter while keeping healthy
checks and demand-triggered probes responsive.

Add rumpel connect to probe the host and pod on demand. Healthy
connections remain untouched. Missing connections are established, and
failed probes replace only the connection that needs repair.

Trigger pending branch pushes when replacement tunnels refresh the
pod's gateway configuration. Publish every initial branch before a new
pod becomes ready so untouched branches are not omitted after removing
recovery work from the events stream.

Cover autonomous recovery for local Docker, SSH, and Kubernetes and
on-demand recovery for Docker and SSH. Verify connect restores a
runtime-added port forward after a daemon restart and a failed pod
without changing its local port.
